  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PhysDisc 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "A research team is discussing a new molecule\u2014a potential target\u2014that
    blocks a protein found in many different types of cells. However, when reviewing
    the team\u2019s findings, you point out that this could cause problems since
    this protein also plays an important role in normal, healthy functions.\nWhy
    is physician input valuable in this situation?"
  explanation: Physicians use their knowledge of how the body works in both health
    and disease to help decide which drug targets are safe and useful. If a target
    is also critical for normal body functions, blocking it could cause serious side
    effects that outweigh any potential benefits. By giving this input early, physicians
    help research teams keep the focus on targets that are not only promising in
    the lab, but also practical and safe for real people.
  correctAnswer: 'B: To make sure the research team avoids targets that could cause
    harmful side effects'
  incorrectAnswer1: 'A: To determine when the first safety studies should be conducted
    in animals'
  incorrectAnswer2: 'C: To redesign the chemical structure of the potential target'
  incorrectAnswer3: 'D: To decide which lab methods should be used to test the compound
    in cell cultures'
  questionRole: Physician
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
